    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "sharepoint_id": "21",
      "title": "Sustainable Development Goals: Yes, we can!",
      "description": "The Times Higher Education ranking has placed Aga Khan University in first place in Pakistan and in the top 5% globally for its contributions to SDG 3 - good health and well-being.",
      "date": "Jun 15, 2022",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Dr Anil Khamis",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "21-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The United Nation's Sustainable Development Goals, SDGs, are a global commitment of the international community that aspire to improve all people's quality of life in such a way that does not compromise future generations' development. The 17 SDGs can be thought of as the 5 Ps: People, Planet, Prosperity, Peace, and Partnerships."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The latest "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Times Higher Education (THE) ranking",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.timeshighereducation.com/rankings/impact/2022/good-health-and-well-being#%21/page/0/length/25/sort_by/rank/sort_order/asc/cols/undefined",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " of 1,100 universities placed AKU in first place in Pakistan and in the top 5% globally for its contributions to SDG 3 - health and well-being. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The THE rankings consider the impact of higher education institutions looking particularly at research, students, and collaborations with service providers."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "AKU's engagement with the SDGs goes back many years and the very establishment of the university and its IQRA mandate - Impact, Quality, Relevance, and Access - not only align to the goals of a better world but have significantly contributed to the setting of these goals. This speaks to the challenge provided by the Chancellor His Highness the Aga Khan in his speech upon accepting the university charter in 1983: \"In everything we do we must look to the future, seeking always to think creatively, to innovate and to improve.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Particular mention can be made of AKU colleagues' research and advocacy, which have contributed to the creation of the World Health Organisation's Nurturing Care Framework (NCF) that aims to ensure all children from the ages of zero to eight years not just  survive but thrive - referred to as early childhood development (ECD) and  Universalisation of Healthcare and Insurance bridging primary and tertiary health care with the creation of knowledge with the requisite human resource capacity building. These innovative approaches respond to the contexts AKU serves, with its sister agencies in the Aga Khan Development Network, and highlight the importance of working in an integrated manner. With the Aga Khan Health Services and the Aga Khan Education Services, the work of the university directly addresses in addition to SDG 3 'Health and Well-Being': SDG 1 'Poverty Alleviation', SDG 2 'Zero Hunger', SDG 4 'Quality Education', and SDG 6 'Gender Equality' and extend to other SDGs.  The two examples above can be supplemented with many more that are innovative, award-winning, and have changed the lives of many people. "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The SDG lens provides universities measurable indicators to show progress and identify gaps in our knowledge that we need to fill. With increasing recognition of AKU's leadership in scholarship and excellence in programmes that meet the needs of the people it serves, opportunities present themselves for the university and its partners, particularly the AKDN, governmental and non-governmental agencies, and development partners to position itself as a contributor and key resource for ongoing transformation that is needed in which research and knowledge production is the urgent and critical need of the day."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Today as we confront climate change and loss of lives and livelihoods with increased heat stress, the rise in anxiety and violent conflict, and apparently limited prospects for our youth who face fast-paced changes spurred by new technologies, we can take heart that AKU is at the forefront of creating new knowledge and has collaborators who are willing partners who envision a hopeful future for all."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
